Keep disc images in memory: IsoImage::preload copies a byte range of the image into
memory on a background thread; reads of that range come from memory once the copy has
passed them. Setting system.disc_in_memory (DISC_IN_MEMORY) preloads the whole disc
image at start (hle_io register_io). For slow drives. (2026-11-24)

